opi-ai — Private WebSocket client protocol modules

This crate links against the following unmodified crates.io dependencies:

- libz-rs-sys 0.6.8 (Zlib) — C-compatible FFI surface over the
  pure-Rust zlib-rs implementation, used with default-features = false and
  the "std" + "rust-allocator" features. The decoder calls the public but
  doc(hidden) inflateSyncPoint / inflateResetKeep exports (the zlib-rs
  __internal-api surface). No source patches, private symbols, custom
  allocators or callbacks are used.
- zlib-rs 0.6.8 (Zlib) — transitive Rust deflate/inflate
  implementation backing libz-rs-sys.
- flate2 1.1.10 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — used with default-features = false and
  the "zlib-rs" backend for the encoder. The optional feature unions
  "union-default" (flate2/default unified with the selected zlib-rs backend) and
  "union-c-zlib" (flate2/zlib, native C libz-sys build) are caller-side
  rehearsals of the supported published feature graphs; every graph keeps the
  direct libz-rs-sys Rust decoder path.

flate2 1.1.10 selects a C backend before zlib-rs, and zlib-rs before
miniz_oxide. The default feature union adds miniz_oxide to the dependency
graph but retains the zlib-rs encoder; the C-zlib union selects libz-sys.

Unsupported feature unions (rejected, not silently accepted): libz-rs-sys
rust-allocator + c-allocator (upstream compile_error!), gz/gzprintf paths,
nightly-only features, export-symbols/prefix combinations, and any other
backend/debug/fuzz combination not listed above. C-zlib native
source/build/link identity (libz-sys toolchain, flags, static archive) is
recorded by the packaging proof, not assumed.

Any upgrade of these dependencies requires the recorded unsafe-boundary,
feature-graph and acceptance reviews to be re-run before adoption (see
README.md, "Maintenance boundaries").
